# What must never enter a build context.
#
# There was no .dockerignore, and `docker build` sends the whole directory to
# the daemon regardless of .gitignore. A COPY of a whole services/ subtree
# therefore baked in the operator's live secrets: review-secrets/ holds a
# project's real .env, auth.json and keys.json so the reviewer can run tests
# that need them. An image is a tarball anyone can `docker save` and unpack,
# and a pushed one is public.
#
# Deny by category rather than by filename, because the next secret to appear
# will have a name nobody predicted here.

# --- secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!docker/.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.key
*.pem
**/keys/
**/review-secrets/
**/*secret*
.initial-admin-password

# --- operator-specific configuration --------------------------------------
projects.json
**/builtin-projects.local.js
services/model-router/config.yaml
scripts/watchdog-services.json

# --- state, logs and other machines' working copies ------------------------
**/worktrees/
**/state.json
**/history.jsonl
**/usage.jsonl
logs/
**/logs/
archives/
dist/
data/
memory/*.md
!memory/*.example.md

# --- build output and dependencies, which every Dockerfile installs itself --
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
site/dist/

# --- version control and local tooling -------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.claude/
*.qcow2
*.iso
